{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Final report (Phase 2 complete — landed & closed)\n\n**Problem.** `record_call_spend` (LLM spend accounting) was silently skipped when\n`finalize_outcome` raised in `PydanticAIRunner.run()` — a call that already burned tokens left\nno spend row.\n\n**Proven root cause.** In `PydanticAIRunner.run()` (src/rebar/llm/runner.py) the finalization\ntail ran `log_call_success` → `finalize_outcome` → `_merge_success_run_shape` →\n`record_call_spend`, with `record_call_spend` as the *last, unguarded* statement after the\nProviderSession `with` and the agent-call `try/except/finally` had exited. A raise from\n`finalize_outcome` (schema validation on a structured/verify_completion call whose model call\nalready succeeded) propagated straight out before `record_call_spend` ran. `log_call_success`\nfires beforehand, so the loss was silent.\n\n**Proof (discriminating, runtime).** The c465 characterization test monkeypatched\n`finalize_outcome` to raise and captured `record_call_spend`: the success log fired yet\n`spend_calls == []`. Demanding exactly one spend row made it RED (`0 == 1`) for precisely this\nmechanism, GREEN after the fix. Mutation check (re-introduce the unguarded ordering, run under\nan OS sandbox) returned it to RED — the test has teeth.\n\n**Defect origin.** `caused_by = 8455-a818-f305-4748` (bug \"record usage for a failed LLM\ncall\", commits c179971eab2d / fc3fc19787a6), `close_class = preexisting`. Attribution by\nscope-of-work: 8455 introduced the failure-path spend contract but only covered the agent-call\nexcept boundary; this finalize boundary is the mirror gap it never reached. No commit *broke*\nworking behavior (the finalize-raise path never recorded spend → omission, not regression); the\nordering predates the ADR-0056 extraction (`8b44b5aa50ee`, \"pure relocation\"). `caused_by` edge\nrecorded on close via `--caused-by`.\n\n**Test (RED→GREEN, held out).**\n`tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py::test_a_raise_in_finalize_outcome_still_logs_and_records_the_spend_row`\n(renamed from the c465 characterization test per AC #2). Seen RED first, GREEN after; held out\nfrom the fix.\n\n**Fix.** Wrapped `finalize_outcome` + the success-only tail (`result[\"_usage\"] = usage`,\n`_merge_success_run_shape(...)`) in a `try:`, and moved `record_call_spend(...)` into a\n`finally:`. On the success path the finally still runs last (after the shape merge), so the\nsuccess spend row is byte-identical incl. run-shape enrichment; on a finalize raise the\nsuccess statements are skipped, the finally records the token-count spend row, and the original\nexception propagates unchanged (disposition preserved). runner.py stays at 797 LOC (< 800 cap).\n\n**Scope & safety.** Single call site for `record_call_spend` (the run() chokepoint) → no\nconstruct siblings; fake/override runners burn no tokens → no parity siblings. Caller-dependency\nsweep: nothing relied on the absence of a spend row on this path (only the c465 characterization\ntest pinned the gap, updated here). Restoration not creation; no new dependency; the touched\ntest was strengthened (gap → fix), not weakened.\n\n**Siblings.** None (Axis 1 construct sweep: single chokepoint; Axis 2 parity census: no other\ntoken-burning surface).\n\n**Residual risk & prevention.** None observed with a citation beyond this fix.\n\n**Replication.** Original report no longer reproduces: `make lint` + `make typecheck` + full\nsuite green locally; Gerrit change **2417** landed with `LLM-Review +1` AND `Verified +1`\n(GitHub Actions run 33296445574 all green: macOS + ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 pytest, lint,\ntypecheck, bounded mutation gate), then plain Submit → MERGED.\n\n**Change:** https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2417 — closed `preexisting`,\n`caused_by 8455-a818-f305-4748`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788072939097741996,"uuid":"951e33c2-c66d-48d0-9b09-3e7b52e14c41"}